Track 1: Ribbons of Baked Magnetite
- Story & Context: Outside the salt-crusted trading post of El Oasis, a convoy of synth-smugglers accidentally ran over a crate of 1950s magnetic recording tape, pressing the dark oxide ribbon deep into the hot asphalt. Park Ji-woo scraped the ruined tape off the road with a hunting knife and spliced it back together, discovering that the friction of dust against the magnetic head played a haunting, rhythmic scratch that locked perfectly into a passing tractor's diesel thump. As the sun set, she sang her first bilingual desert lament over the crackling tape loops, coining the phrase that would start the movement. "The sun ate my cassette before I could say I loved you," she purred into a battered radio transmitter.
